WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:12,070
My two were bled on Monday and I couldn't stop it.

00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:15,290
We went to the ER and still at the hospital.

00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:17,170
This person, I hope you saw in that questions

00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:20,750
that we answered last week.

00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:23,670
I am starting my first radiation treatment this afternoon.

00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:25,350
Oh, that is fantastic.

00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:26,810
That is great.

00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:28,390
Glad to hear that.

00:00:28,390 --> 00:00:31,390
They are suggesting radiation and chemo together

00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:33,670
or what are your thoughts about chemo.

00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:36,870
You really want to talk to the oncologists

00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:41,750
and say, OK, well, I know you want me to do chemo.

00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,230
How was that going to give me any better chance?

00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:46,430
There's nothing wrong with pinpointing them down.

00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:50,390
They won't let us give any statistics

00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:53,670
because they're the gods that have all the statistics.

00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:56,550
Well, then pass them the statistics.

00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:59,510
How do you think this is going to actually improve my life?

00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,670
Is this going to, you're saying this, if I do chemo,

00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:04,550
you're going to give me another month to live.

00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:07,350
But I'm going to live a horrific existence for that month

00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:08,390
because I'm going to be so sick.

00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:11,630
So just ask them those pin-pointed questions.

00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:13,790
They're the ones asking you to do something that's

00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:14,950
going to make you sick.

00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:17,790
So you have the right to ask them those questions.

